I've completed the bootstrap task for the MotionEngine repository. Here's what I've done:

1. Created the complete project structure with all required files:
   - CMakeLists.txt with proper JUCE integration
   - PluginProcessor.h/cpp and PluginEditor.h/cpp for the basic plugin structure
   - DSP headers (EnvelopeFollower.h) 
   - Test runner (TestMain.cpp)
   - Build scripts (build.sh, test.sh, validate.sh)
   - Configuration files (CLAUDE.md, TASKS.md, STATE.md)

2. Set up JUCE as a submodule (version 8.0.4)

3. Configured the build system to create both the VST3 plugin and console test executable

4. Made all scripts executable

5. Committed everything with the proper commit message format

The build currently fails because cmake is not installed on the system, but the repository structure is complete and ready for the next steps. The STATE.md file records this bootstrap completion.

The next task (T-02) will be to implement and test the EnvelopeFollower DSP component.
